The changes below make the post cache a lazily created shared singleton, route every consumer through `getOrCreate()`, and extend `Meta.slugTaken` to handle scalar and array input. I have not run the tests.

Two notes on the design:
- `groups.existsBySlug` and `categories.existsByHandle` are in files I was not given, so I map over the slugs and call them once per slug rather than assuming array support.
- `cache.del` on the underlying LRU cache may not accept arrays, so `del` loops over the keys.

`src/webserver.js` has no post cache reference, so I left it unchanged.

