Plain URLs with several underscores inside an emphasised span should now render in full, with no emphasis markup added. I haven't run the tests.

The cause was that link repair in `src/Markdown.ts` only read and cleared the emphasis node's first child. Any text after a nested `__…__` part was lost from the rebuilt link text and left behind inside the emphasis. For example, in `https://example.com/_test__test2__test3_` the span contains `test`, a bold `test2` and `test3`, and only `test` was used.

The changes:
- **New helper `innerNodeLiteral(node)`.** It walks every descendant with the commonmark walker and joins the literals of all `text` nodes on entering steps.
- **`em`/`strong` handling uses the helper.** It uses `innerNodeLiteral(node)` instead of `node.firstChild.literal`, both for the "is there text here" check and to rebuild the segment (e.g. `_test__test2__test3_`) used for link detection.
- **All nested text is cleared.** Every descendant `text` node is now emptied, not just the first child. This stops leftover text being rendered a second time.

