The function accepts a plain ASCII integer as seconds. Otherwise it tokenises `\d+[hms]` pairs and returns -1 unless the tokens rebuild the whole input exactly, with no duplicate units. That rejects the empty string, signs, fractions and stray letters. The result is a summed int in milliseconds, so order doesn't matter.

